  "title": "Provider-neutral tracker seam with a GitHub Issues/Projects adapter",
  "summary": "This change introduces a provider-neutral `Tracker` seam in `crates/osf/src/tracker` — a trait with read/write/capability operations, a ready rule that decides which read item may be dispatched, a finishing-write helper, and an in-memory test double — and adds the first adapter, `GitHubTracker`, which drives GitHub Issues and Projects v2 through the installed `gh` CLI. Every adapter request is one `gh` invocation whose argv and JSON payload are built by pure functions and whose response is read by a pure parser, so the adapter is a thin loop over a `GhRunner` trait that the real runner implements with a timeout.",
  "lenses": [
    "architecture",
    "data-flow"
  ],
